      },
      "worked": "Rewrite $y=2+3(x-1)^{-1}$, so $y'=-3(x-1)^{-2}$. At $x=2$, the point is $(2,5)$ and the tangent gradient is $-3$. The normal gradient is therefore $\\tfrac13$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-5&=\\frac13(x-2)\\\\y&=\\frac13x+\\frac{13}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe intercepts are $X=(-13,0)$ and $Y=(0,\\tfrac{13}{3})$. Using their positive lengths,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area of }\\triangle OXY&=\\frac12\\times13\\times\\frac{13}{3}\\\\&=\\frac{169}{6}\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
